Gap: `Subspace::at`'s `for (&root, &inverse) in self.roots.iter().zip(&self.inverses)` - Aeneas stops on the function (`[Error] Unimplemented`) and the extraction fails
The loop goes by index, up to `self.roots.len()`. The fields are private and `Subspace::new`, the
only constructor, gives `inverses` one entry per root, so the zip ran that far too.
Tests: whir::tests::novel_basis_matches_the_vanishing_products, which compares `at`'s values
with the vanishing polynomials multiplied out; whir::tests::times_x_is_multiplication_by_x and
whir::tests::affine_row_fold_and_high_correction, which go through `at`;
`-p stable_lean_vm_core --test verifiers`.
mutation: the inverses taken in reverse -> the three and the real-proof suite fail.

